  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1210 PM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nAn almost Rex-like blocking pattern holds thru the weekend, with\nthe influx low level flow pattern maintaining north to \nnortheasterlies for the bulk of that period. Satellite and \nsounding data shows extensive moisture reinforcents on the way,\ncited in the soundings lower column up to about 5K (BNA) to 7K \n(ILN) feet holding firm, so BINOVC may be hard to mix to more \nabundant sunshine during this at least near term period, and sky\ncondition/temps have been adjusted to account as the NBM hasn't\nbeen exceptional with its capture. This pattern persistence \nwill keep pleasantly cooler and drier conditions with 70s and \n50s predominant for highs and lows.\n\nThat will be followed by a warmup that ensues for the middle \npart of next week, to more summer-like 80s and 60s for highs and\nlows as the surface influx flow returns to southerlies \ncoincident with the block breaking down. Developing/approaching \ntroffing from the west will likewise return pcpn chances, though\nit is a little early to speculate on strong/svr storm \nchances...but that's the time to look for it as pops start to \nrise with the building heat/humidity and an approaching system \nentering the medium to longer range forecast picture. Noted the\n6-10 and 8-14 day outlooks Above/Above for Temps/Pcpn, so \nperhaps another prolonged duration warmer period is in store if \nit pans out.",
